# Dev Notes 11 — runtime-lifecycle-modularization-v1 runtime lifecycle state container

## Branch

`runtime-lifecycle-modularization-v1-runtime-lifecycle-state-container`

## Status

First lifecycle-state-container slice staged and sandbox/mock verified.

This branch intentionally makes parent runtime lifecycle coordination state explicit without extracting init, reset, shutdown, native-boundary, worker-router, scheduler, workerBridge, or request-settlement behavior into new coordinators.

## Source base

Started from the current `modularization` branch source mirrored by:

```text
runtime-dev-repo-modularization.zip
```

The source base already included:

```text
nativeOperationPolicy.mjs
docs/dev-notes.09
runtimeRequestSettlement.mjs
docs/dev-notes.10
```

Observed source ZIP SHA-256 during prep:

```text
bcedac845914fae443f7ff02d5ed7c5c94bce160a04a6fcbb9ecffb86c792f10
```

## Purpose

Continue lifecycle modularization conservatively by moving parent-runtime lifecycle coordination state out of raw `inference.mjs` module-scope variable declarations into a small explicit state container.

The goal is to prepare later coordinator extractions while preserving current runtime behavior.

## Implementation summary

Added:

```text
runtimeLifecycleState.mjs
```

The new module exports:

```js
export function createRuntimeLifecycleState() { ... }
```

The state container owns only parent lifecycle coordination state:

```text
initStarted
initResolved
initInProgress
initCyclePromise
readyPromise
resolveReady
rejectReady
activeInitAttemptId
activeInitPlan
lastSuccessfulInitPlan
lastSuccessfulEffectiveConfig
lastSuccessfulProbe
lastFailedExplicitInit
nextInitAttemptId
sessionsResetting
sessionResetWaiters
runtimeResetting
runtimeShuttingDown
runtimeUnhealthy
modelResetWaiter
shutdownWaiter
```

It also owns small state-local helpers:

```js
resetReadyBarrier()
resetInitBarrier()
nextAttemptId()
```

`inference.mjs` now imports and instantiates it:

```js
import { createRuntimeLifecycleState } from "./runtimeLifecycleState.mjs";

const lifecycle = createRuntimeLifecycleState();
```

Former direct module-scope lifecycle variables in `inference.mjs` now read/write through `lifecycle.*` properties.

## What intentionally stayed in `inference.mjs`

The following behavior-bearing code remains in `inference.mjs`:

```text
initModel()
ensureModelReady()
runInitCycle()
attemptInitOnce()
createInitPlan()
createFixedInitPlanFromLastSuccess()
worker message routing
runtime unhealthy helpers
native operation boundary waiting
resetSession()
resetModel()
shutdownRuntime()
shutdown mode orchestration
cancelPrompt()
cancellation loops
scheduler creation/ownership
request settlement dependency wiring
public API exports
```

Reason:

- this branch is a state-container seam only;
- lifecycle behavior extraction remains high-risk and should be handled in later narrow coordinator branches;
- scheduler and workerBridge ownership are architecture boundaries and were not moved.

## Behavior preservation notes

No intentional changes to:

```text
public API shape
error text
prompt/output semantics
request settlement order
cancellation ordering
scheduler queue/in-flight ownership
worker lifecycle/replacement behavior
worker operation serialization
configOverride validation
retry/profile planning
hardware probing behavior
native operation timeout/unhealthy policy
shutdown mode semantics
model path/model identity policy
```

Important preserved details:

```text
resetInitBarrier() still leaves scheduler readiness handling explicit in inference.mjs
readyPromise / resolveReady / rejectReady barrier semantics are preserved
initCyclePromise still represents the full init cycle
activeInitAttemptId stale ready/error guards remain in the worker message router
failed explicit custom/profile init still blocks unsafe silent default prompt auto-init
last successful effective config/probe records still drive resetModel() re-init behavior
session reset timeout semantics remain unchanged
modelResetWaiter and shutdownWaiter clear in the same routing/finally paths as before
```

