## Review notes

This branch follows the modularization amendment by introducing the lifecycle state container after the request-settlement helper slice.

The state container deliberately uses a plain factory/object style rather than a class hierarchy. This keeps the change mechanical and consistent with the existing function-oriented module style.

The branch does not yet make `inference.mjs` much smaller. That is intentional. The value is that later coordinator branches can receive an explicit lifecycle object instead of relying on broad module-scope closure state.

## Caveats

- This branch touches many lifecycle state use sites in `inference.mjs`; the change is mechanical but broad.
- Local real-runtime verification is still recommended before merge consideration.
- Fixture propagation remains a recurring risk for every new module imported by `inference.mjs`.
- Prior transient real-runtime shutdown/native-boundary timeout caveats remain visible and were not addressed here.
- This branch does not extract native-boundary behavior, init behavior, reset behavior, shutdown behavior, or worker routing.

